  "strengths": [
    {
      "value": "Largest scope to date: 16 LLMs evaluated on six trust dimensions across 30+ datasets and 18+ subcategories.",
      "ev": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "1 Introduction",
        "quote": "We benchmark 30 datasets to comprehensively evaluate the functional capabilities of LLMs ... evaluating 16 LLMs, encompassing both proprietary and open-source models",
        "bbox": [
          70.224609375,
          461.2157287597656,
          541.7889404296875,
          687.2666625976562
        ],
        "block_id": "/page/5/ListGroup/242"
      }
    },
    {
      "value": "Introduces principled taxonomy with eight trustworthiness facets grounded in a review of 600 papers.",
      "ev": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "1 Introduction",
        "quote": "We conducted an extensive review of 600 papers on LLM trustworthiness ... identified eight key aspects ... truthfulness, safety, fairness, robustness, privacy, machine ethics, transparency, and accountability",
        "bbox": [
          70.224609375,
          461.2157287597656,
          541.7889404296875,
          687.2666625976562
        ],
        "block_id": "/page/5/ListGroup/242"
      }
    },
    {
      "value": "Releases new datasets (Jailbreak Trigger 1300 prompts, AdvInstruction, Misuse Additional) along with code and a public leaderboard.",
      "ev": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "ABSTRACT",
        "quote": "Our dataset, code, and toolkit will be available at https://github.com/HowieHwong/TrustLLM and the leaderboard is released at https://trustllmbenchmark.github.io/TrustLLM-Website/",
        "bbox": [
          106.083984375,
          92.0390625,
          506.0743713378906,
          652.9306488037109
        ],
        "block_id": "/page/1/Text/2"
      }
    },
    {
      "value": "Reveals important trade-off between safety and utility: stronger safety alignment correlates with exaggerated refusals, e.g. Llama2-7b refuses 49% of benign prompts.",
      "ev": {
        "page": 9,
        "section": "2.1 Overall Observations",
